# CL-7 Stage C item 14: the policy a visitor's browser enforces on DueWeave. Every origin
# here is one the app loads (measured in `client/index.html` and the production build script),
# every concession is paid for by a feature, and `tests/response-headers.contract.test.ts`
# re-derives both from the sources so this file cannot drift quietly.
#
# CL-7 P3 item 12 adds the CAPTCHA host, and it is the one third-party script this product
# runs: `client/src/lib/turnstile.ts` loads it explicitly, and the widget it renders lives in
# a child frame from the same origin. Both halves have to be allowed or enabling the hosted
# GoTrue CAPTCHA would break sign-in instead of protecting it. `frame-ancestors 'none'` stays
# exactly where it was — admitting a child frame is not admitting that DueWeave gets framed.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://ugzdqcytouwfdlcjujqv.supabase.co wss://ugzdqcytouwfdlcjujqv.supabase.co; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
